<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Partial Info.plist: Xcode merges the generated keys into this file because
	     GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE stays YES. It lives outside the Sber/ folder on
	     purpose — that folder is a synchronized group, and a plist inside it would
	     also be copied in as a resource. -->
	<!-- Without this, App Transport Security blocks the plain-http calls to the
	     local FastAPI backend. -->
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
	<!-- Needed on a real device: since iOS 14 reaching a backend on the local
	     network (the Mac running uvicorn) asks the user for permission, and
	     without this string the prompt has nothing to show. On the simulator
	     localhost needs none of this. -->
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Приложение обращается к серверу поддержки в вашей локальной сети, чтобы отправлять обращения и получать ответы.</string>
	<!-- Dictation in the support chat. Without both of these iOS kills the app the
	     moment the microphone button is tapped. -->
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Микрофон нужен, чтобы описать проблему голосом вместо набора текста.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Распознавание речи превращает ваше голосовое обращение в текст, который вы сможете проверить перед отправкой.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
